# tools/p/port_band_witness.rish -- the room's port numbers, counted off the sources.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. A port is a name on the MACHINE, and this pier stands eight checkouts deep whose
# roster passes overlap almost entirely. REDS %700 is the bill: a rostered witness read red on one
# cold pass and green on a re-run over an unchanged tree, and the cause took a fortnight to name --
# two lawful runs reached one compiled-in UDP port and each read the other's replies. Proven on
# metal `20260911` at load 14, eight at once: the elder binary 39 of 80 red, the repaired binary 0
# of 80, and both 0 of 120 run serially. A fault that appears only in company is a fault one run
# alone will always miss.
#
# WHY A METER RATHER THAN ANOTHER SENTENCE. The room already had an answer and wrote it in prose.
# Two lock scripts serialize the runs that share a pair, and each spells its room's roster in its
# own header -- *seven modules under mantra/ bind 38478/38479 through 38490/38491*, and
# *amphora/vessel_fetch_delivery.rye binds UDP 38494 and 38495*. Both sentences were true when they
# were typed, and both went stale the moment a module was repaired. The tablecloth delivery module
# took the bind-to-zero handshake on `20260911.105415` and let 38490/38491 go; the amphora fetcher
# let 38494 go, and `linengrow/neth_serial_core_delivery.rye` declares it today. A sentence holding
# a roster is a roster a hand must re-type, and this tree's own law already names the cure: COUNT,
# NEVER NUMBER (`.claude/rules/stamp-and-name.md`). So the roster is read off the declarations, and
# each sentence points here.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal.
#   Every `const <name>: u16 = <number>;` in living tracked Rye where `port` is a whole component
#     of the identifier, so `wire_port` counts and `max_report` is read past. A port of 0 is the
#     CURE, named apart and charged to nothing.
#   A constant outside the room's seated band `38472-38600`, held at ZERO. The floor is the first
#     number this room seated and the ceiling leaves the counting-up convention room to grow, so a
#     module reaching for 8080 at random reds on the lap it arrives.
#   A lock whose numeric edge check would refuse a port its own room declares, held at ZERO. The
#     next module past a lock's band is caught by this reading, where before it would have met a
#     closed door at the lock itself. The comparison runs against each port that OPENS a pair,
#     since a lock is taken on the low port: the first draft compared every declared port and
#     reported a fault against a correct file, which is the one failure a guard cannot afford.
#   One number declared by two modules, under a ceiling that only falls. THREE stand today --
#     38495, 38496 and 38497, six declarations across four files, each lawful for its own module
#     and a collision for the pier. Each repair is a choice of number inside another lane, so the
#     three are NAMED for their owners and left for those hands.
#   A SECOND ROOM, IN A SECOND LANGUAGE (`20260911`). The wire labs carrying these same
#     capabilities onto virtio declare their ports in RISHI, as the default half of an environment
#     override -- `if port_request_raw == "" then let port_request = "15561"` -- so a reading of
#     `const <name>: u16` passed over 29 declarations across 15 labs. Three readings answer it, each
#     a WALL at zero rather than a ratchet: a lab default outside the seated device band
#     `15555-15600`; one number claimed by two labs; and ONE OVERRIDE NAME READ BY TWO LABS, which
#     is the reading a census of numbers alone would have missed -- the escape hatch sharing the
#     collision it exists to escape. Before the repair: five numbers doubled and four overrides
#     shared, and they were the same four labs, each made by copying a sibling while the port block
#     travelled unread. Four mantra labs moved to 15577-15584 and no other lane's file was touched.
#   Eighty behaviors on real git repositories in a throwaway pen: every refusal planted then
#     lifted and read as zero, every ceiling shown from both sides, and FOUR mutations each biting
#     their own leg -- the pair-high rule, the whole-component rule shown biting BOTH halves since
#     it is written once and read by both, and the `sort -u` that keeps one lab naming its own
#     variable twice from reading as two labs sharing it -- since a rule nothing depends on is a
#     rule that may quietly stop working.
#
# WHAT THIS LEAVES WHOLE, and the number that says why it matters.
#   WHETHER two modules ever actually MEET on a number. That depends on which ships run which guard
#     at which second, and `tools/fixtures/m/mantra_delivery_port_control.sh` proves that half in
#     company. This rung proves the SHAPE that lets the meeting happen.
#   THE HOST. Read on this pier `20260911`, `/proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_local_port_range` answers
#     `32768 60999` and `ip_local_reserved_ports` is EMPTY, so every number in the seated band is
#     one the kernel may hand any client socket on this machine at any moment. The band orders our
#     own modules, and the host remains free. A one-line `ip_local_reserved_ports` reservation
#     would settle it, and that is a host configuration -- authored in `nixos/` and copied out
#     (`.claude/rules/declared-host-config.md`), which makes it Keaton's.
#   A base a module counts UP from claims a span a literal census reads past. Two stand --
#     `comlink/rehearsal_wire.rye` at 38498, one per ship, and `constel/socket.rye` at 38512, one
#     per seat -- so `band_free` is printed beside `counting_bases` and read together with it.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/p/port_band_witness.rish

say "port-band: Language EN -- a port is a name on the machine, and eight checkouts share one machine."
say "port-band: Style Gauge, Meter -- refusal is the subject."
say "port-band: Lens TAME -- safety first: a number two modules claim is a reply one of them reads wrongly."
say "port-band: and a roster that reads one language reports the language, never the tree."

# THE CAPTURE IS SAID ONCE, BARE, ABOVE THE ASSERTS THAT READ IT. Rishi composes an interpolated
# `assert ... else` into one 4,096-byte strbuf, so an else clause repeating a reading the bare `say`
# two lines up already printed costs that buffer on the failing path and hands a reader nothing new
# -- the shape `tools/fixtures/s/say_compose_bound_scan.sh` counts as `deferred` (BAKERY,
# `20260911`, closing that guard's 490-against-489 red).
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/port_band_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "port-band: a reading stands past its gate -- the scan's whole reading stands above this line"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "port-band: the scan must balance before it is believed -- its whole reading stands above this line"
assert scan.out contains "ports_outside_band=0" else "port-band: a constant outside the seated band is a number picked at random -- the reading above names the file"
assert scan.out contains "lock_band_uncovered=0" else "port-band: a lock refusing a port its own room declares turns away the caller it protects -- the reading above names the lock"
assert scan.out contains "device_ports_outside_band=0" else "port-band: a lab default outside the seated device band is a number picked at random -- the reading above names the lab"
assert scan.out contains "device_double_claimed=0" else "port-band: one device number claimed by two labs is one QEMU listen address two runs reach -- the reading above names both"
assert scan.out contains "device_override_shared=0" else "port-band: an override two labs read moves both at once, so it separates nothing -- the reading above names it"
say "device GREEN -- every lab default stands inside the seated device band, each number is one lab's, and each override moves one lab"
say "field GREEN -- every constant port stands inside the seated band, and every lock covers its own room"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/p/port_band_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "port-band: the control must complete -- its whole output stands above this line"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "port-band: a control leg refused, so no reading below is believable -- the failing leg names itself above"
assert control.out contains "clean_reads_zero=yes" else "port-band: a clean tree must read zero rather than merely pass"
assert control.out contains "clean_free=yes" else "port-band: a clean tree must pass free"
assert control.out contains "inside_band_counted=yes" else "port-band: a lawful constant port must still be counted"
assert control.out contains "outside_band_counted=yes" else "port-band: a port outside the band must be counted"
assert control.out contains "outside_band_refused=yes" else "port-band: a port outside the band must refuse"
assert control.out contains "outside_band_named=yes" else "port-band: the refusal must name a verdict, never only an exit code"
assert control.out contains "outside_file_named=yes" else "port-band: the reading must name the file, so the repair is one line away"
assert control.out contains "outside_band_lifted=yes" else "port-band: lifting the plant must return the reading to zero"
assert control.out contains "zero_port_named=yes" else "port-band: a kernel-chosen port must be named apart"
assert control.out contains "zero_port_uncharged=yes" else "port-band: the cure must never be charged as the fault"
assert control.out contains "zero_port_free=yes" else "port-band: a port of 0 is inside no band"
assert control.out contains "substring_free=yes" else "port-band: max_report holds the letters and holds no port"
assert control.out contains "pub_counted=yes" else "port-band: a pub prefix changes nothing about who holds the number"
assert control.out contains "testimony_free=yes" else "port-band: dated testimony binds no port on this pier"
assert control.out contains "testimony_absent=yes" else "port-band: a freed declaration must be absent from the listing, not merely uncounted"
assert control.out contains "double_counted=yes" else "port-band: one number declared by two modules must be counted"
assert control.out contains "double_named=yes" else "port-band: both claimants must be named"
assert control.out contains "double_at_ceiling_free=yes" else "port-band: a double set at its ceiling must pass free"
assert control.out contains "double_over_ceiling_refused=yes" else "port-band: a double set past its ceiling must refuse"
assert control.out contains "double_over_named=yes" else "port-band: the ceiling refusal must name its verdict"
assert control.out contains "free_excludes_claimed=yes" else "port-band: a claimed number is never offered as free"
assert control.out contains "free_includes_unclaimed=yes" else "port-band: the free list must not become empty by accident"
assert control.out contains "base_reported=yes" else "port-band: a base that counts up claims a span no literal census sees"
assert control.out contains "lock_found=yes" else "port-band: a lock is found by the name shape this room writes"
assert control.out contains "lock_pair_high_free=yes" else "port-band: a lock is taken on the low port, so the high half of a pair is never handed to it"
assert control.out contains "lock_covering_free=yes" else "port-band: a lock covering its own room must pass free"
assert control.out contains "lock_uncovered_counted=yes" else "port-band: a pair opening past a lock's band must be counted"
assert control.out contains "lock_uncovered_refused=yes" else "port-band: a pair opening past a lock's band must refuse"
assert control.out contains "lock_uncovered_named=yes" else "port-band: the refusal must name its verdict"
assert control.out contains "lock_uncovered_port_named=yes" else "port-band: the refusal must name the port, so the band is one edit away"
assert control.out contains "lock_uncovered_lifted=yes" else "port-band: lifting the plant must return the reading to zero"
assert control.out contains "lock_no_edge_free=yes" else "port-band: a lock bounding no range refuses nothing and is read past"
assert control.out contains "lock_own_number_free=yes" else "port-band: a lock naming its own room's port claims nothing stale"
assert control.out contains "lock_no_edge_verdict_ok=yes" else "port-band: a lock with no edge check must leave the verdict alone"
assert control.out contains "lock_unbound_counted=yes" else "port-band: a number a lock's own room let go must be reported"
assert control.out contains "lock_unbound_named=yes" else "port-band: the stale number and its lock must both be named"
assert control.out contains "lock_unbound_reported_not_gated=yes" else "port-band: a reading the owning lane must judge is reported, never gated"
assert control.out contains "lock_unbound_lifted=yes" else "port-band: declaring the number again must return the reading to zero"
assert control.out contains "no_root_refused=yes" else "port-band: a root that is not a directory must refuse"
assert control.out contains "no_git_refused=yes" else "port-band: a root that is not a checkout must refuse"
assert control.out contains "no_sources_refused=yes" else "port-band: a tree with no Rye source must refuse rather than read zero"
assert control.out contains "mutation_pair_high_bites=yes" else "port-band: removing the pair-high rule must report a fault against a correct file"
assert control.out contains "mutation_substring_bites=yes" else "port-band: removing the whole-component rule must read max_report as a port"
assert control.out contains "mutation_substring_reds_clean=yes" else "port-band: the extra reading must be a fault rather than a harmless count"
assert control.out contains "device_no_lab_counted=yes" else "port-band: a tree with no wire lab must be counted rather than guessed"
assert control.out contains "device_no_lab_zero=yes" else "port-band: no lab means no declaration"
assert control.out contains "device_no_lab_free=yes" else "port-band: the labs are a room this tree grew, so a tree without them passes free"
assert control.out contains "device_lab_found=yes" else "port-band: a lab is found by the name shape this room writes"
assert control.out contains "device_inside_counted=yes" else "port-band: a lawful lab default must still be counted"
assert control.out contains "device_inside_free=yes" else "port-band: a lawful lab default sits inside the band"
assert control.out contains "device_lawful_lab_free=yes" else "port-band: a lawful lab must pass free"
assert control.out contains "device_outside_counted=yes" else "port-band: a lab default outside the device band must be counted"
assert control.out contains "device_outside_refused=yes" else "port-band: a lab default outside the device band must refuse"
assert control.out contains "device_outside_named=yes" else "port-band: the refusal must name a verdict, never only an exit code"
assert control.out contains "device_outside_file_named=yes" else "port-band: the reading must name the lab, so the repair is one line away"
assert control.out contains "device_outside_lifted=yes" else "port-band: lifting the plant must return the reading to zero"
assert control.out contains "device_double_counted=yes" else "port-band: one device number claimed by two labs must be counted"
assert control.out contains "device_double_refused=yes" else "port-band: a device double must refuse, since its ceiling is zero"
assert control.out contains "device_double_named=yes" else "port-band: the device double refusal must name its verdict"
assert control.out contains "device_double_claimant_named=yes" else "port-band: both claimant labs must be named"
assert control.out contains "device_double_at_ceiling_free=yes" else "port-band: a device double set at its ceiling must pass free"
assert control.out contains "device_double_lifted=yes" else "port-band: lifting the plant must return the reading to zero"
assert control.out contains "device_override_numbers_differ=yes" else "port-band: the override leg must plant labs whose numbers differ, so it can only pass by reading the name"
assert control.out contains "device_override_counted=yes" else "port-band: one override name read by two labs must be counted"
assert control.out contains "device_override_refused=yes" else "port-band: a shared override must refuse, since its ceiling is zero"
assert control.out contains "device_override_named=yes" else "port-band: the shared-override refusal must name its verdict"
assert control.out contains "device_override_name_named=yes" else "port-band: the shared variable must be named, so a hand knows what to rename"
assert control.out contains "device_override_site_named=yes" else "port-band: both reading labs must be named"
assert control.out contains "device_override_lifted=yes" else "port-band: lifting the plant must return the reading to zero"
assert control.out contains "device_substring_free=yes" else "port-band: a lab variable merely carrying the letters holds no port"
assert control.out contains "device_lab_counted_anyway=yes" else "port-band: a lab declaring no port is still a lab"
assert control.out contains "device_free_includes_unclaimed=yes" else "port-band: the device free list must not become empty by accident"
assert control.out contains "device_free_excludes_claimed=yes" else "port-band: a claimed device number is never offered as free"
assert control.out contains "device_listed=yes" else "port-band: --list must name every device declaration"
assert control.out contains "device_self_named_free=yes" else "port-band: one lab naming its own variable twice is not two labs"
assert control.out contains "mutation_substring_bites_device=yes" else "port-band: removing the whole-component rule must read a lab passport as a port"
assert control.out contains "mutation_override_dedupe_applied=yes" else "port-band: the dedupe mutation must actually change the scan it mutates"
assert control.out contains "mutation_override_dedupe_bites=yes" else "port-band: removing the override dedupe must report a fault against a correct lab"
assert control.out contains "behaviors=80" else "port-band: the control must run every behavior this witness names"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=proven" else "port-band: the control must agree with itself"
say "RED and GREEN paths proven -- six refusals bitten across two rooms, every free rule planted then read as zero, and four mutations each biting their own leg"

say "GREEN: port-band -- every port number this room writes down is counted in BOTH languages it writes them in, the Rye delivery constants and the Rishi lab defaults, and the roster is read rather than re-typed."
